{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a transition-metal-free, visible-light-induced radical hydrodifluoromethylation of alkenes using the phosphonium salt [Ph3P+CF2H]Br- as the difluoromethyl source. The reaction is promoted by a Hantzsch ester and Ph2SiH2 under 26 W household compact fluorescent light (CFL), providing a mild and operationally simple method for constructing Csp3-CF2H bonds with broad functional group tolerance.",
